    "title": "Straight answers",
    "items": [
     {
      "q": "Does it file my return for me?",
      "a": "No — and that is deliberate. TaxCheck never submits anything to the FTA. It prepares, checks, and shows its work; you review, approve, and file. You are the one signing the return, so you are the one who decides what goes in it."
     },
     {
      "q": "Can I trust AI with tax figures?",
      "a": "It does not calculate — it reads. Every figure is copied exactly as printed on the document, then recomputed and cross-checked by our engine. When something does not reconcile, you get a flag showing both numbers — never a silent correction. It will refuse to invent an exchange rate rather than guess one."
     },
     {
      "q": "What happens when it gets something wrong?",
      "a": "It tells you. On our first real batch of 19 invoices, 16 were read perfectly and all three hard cases — a USD export, an invoice split across two pages, and a duplicate from an older batch — were flagged for review. Zero silent errors. That last number is the one that matters."
     },
     {
      "q": "Is it really free?",
      "a": "Yes, during early access — no card, no sales call. We are building this alongside accountants working on real returns, and right now your feedback is worth more to us than your subscription."
     },
     {
      "q": "Does it replace my accountant?",
      "a": "No — it is built for accountants. It removes the typing and the cross-checking. The judgment stays with you."
